<<<
orography, orolingual, &c. The identical representation of Greek oros mountain & Latin os mouth by oro- is regrettable.
===
**orography, orolingual,** &c. The identical representation of Greek *oros* mountain & Latin *os* mouth by *oro-* is regrettable.
>>>

<<<
The most convenient arrangement consistent with correctness would have been to make ori- the combining form of Latin os mouth (oricentral, ori-anal, orilingual, &c.), & oreo- that of Greek oros mountain (oreography, oreometric, &c.).
===
The most convenient arrangement consistent with correctness would have been to make *ori-* the combining form of Latin *os* mouth (*oricentral, ori-anal, orilingual,* &c.), & *oreo-* that of Greek *oros* mountain (*oreography, oreometric,* &c.).
>>>

<<<
As ori- does exist in orinasal & other mouth-words, & oreo- has not been entirely superseded in the mountain-words, it is possibly not too late to suggest that this distinction should even now be established.
===
As *ori-* does exist in *orinasal* & other mouth-words, & *oreo-* has not been entirely superseded in the mountain-words, it is possibly not too late to suggest that this distinction should even now be established.
>>>

